{"surface": "event", "title": "Bitcoin falls below $50,000 by May 18, 2027", "html": "<div class=\"ev ws\"><div class=\"evh\"><h2 class=\"title\">Bitcoin falls below $50,000 by May 18, 2027</h2><p class=\"facts\"><span>Any time to May 18, 2027</span><span class=\"sep\">·</span><span class=\"src\">Known from Bitcoin spot price on major exchanges (Binance BTC/USDT, Coinbase)</span></p><div class=\"hds\"><details class=\"hd\" data-k=\"definition\"><summary>Definition</summary><div class=\"hdb text\"><p>Bitcoin trades below $50,000 at any time from November 19, 2026 through May 18, 2027. It stood near $63,000 on November 19, about 27% below its October 4 close of $86,475.</p></div></details><details class=\"hd\" data-k=\"notes\"><summary>Rationale</summary><div class=\"hdb\"><div class=\"note\" data-k=\"note:64\" data-note=\"note:64\"><div class=\"md\" data-md=\"The year-end markets (Kalshi 0.265, Polymarket 0.22) price a 21% fall inside six weeks, which is a volatility near 58% a year. Carried to May 18 at that volatility with no drift, the chance of touching $50,000 is about 0.57; volatility this high rarely lasts six months, so I use about 0.50 for the whole window, which leaves 0.34 for the months after December given no touch before.\"><p>The year-end markets (Kalshi 0.265, Polymarket 0.22) price a 21% fall inside six weeks, which is a volatility near 58% a year. Carried to May 18 at that volatility with no drift, the chance of touching $50,000 is about 0.57; volatility this high rarely lasts six months, so I use about 0.50 for the whole window, which leaves 0.34 for the months after December given no touch before.</p></div></div></div></details></div></div><div class=\"strip\" data-count=\"6\" style=\"--cols:5\"><div class=\"sf first\" data-k=\"fig:Forecast\"><span class=\"lab\">Forecast</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:p:prop:7\"><span class=\"n v\">51.5%</span></a></span><a class=\"cap go calc\" data-go=\"x:p:prop:7\">How it’s set →</a></d